      "description": "Job & Internship | Discover Opportunities – Apply Now — Boricua College 0 Skip to Content ADMISSIONS FINANCIAL AID ACADEMICS Registration, Tuition & Fees Five Ways of Learning Academic Programs Student Resources Faculty Transcript Request Scholarships Online Bookstore HEOP Project RISE Mental Health - Here to Help Job & Internship ADMINISTRATION Manhattan Campus Transition Administration Administrative Resources CARES Act Reports Board of Trustees WORK @ BORICUA SCHOOL STORE QUE PASA Academic Calendar Que Pasa Media Commencement 2026 Commencement 2025 Commencement 2024 Class of 2023 DONATE Apply Now Open Menu Close Menu ADMISSIONS FINANCIAL AID ACADEMICS Registration, Tuition & Fees Five Ways of Learning Academic Programs Student Resources Faculty Transcript Request Scholarships Online Bookstore HEOP Project RISE Mental Health - Here to Help Job & Internship ADMINISTRATION Manhattan Campus Transition Administration Administrative Resources CARES Act Reports Board of Trustees WORK @ BORICUA SCHOOL STORE QUE PASA Academic Calendar Que Pasa Media Commencement 2026 Commencement 2025 Commencement 2024 Class of 2023 DONATE Apply Now Open Menu Close Menu ADMISSIONS FINANCIAL AID Folder: ACADEMICS Back Registration, Tuition & Fees Five Ways of Learning Academic Programs Student Resources Faculty Transcript Request Scholarships Online Bookstore HEOP Project RISE Mental Health - Here to Help Job & Internship Folder: ADMINISTRATION Back Manhattan Campus Transition Administration Administrative Resources CARES Act Reports Board of Trustees WORK @ BORICUA SCHOOL STORE Folder: QUE PASA Back Academic Calendar Que Pasa Media Commencement 2026 Commencement 2025 Commencement 2024 Class of 2023 DONATE Apply Now JOB & INTERNSHIP BOARD EXTERNAL JOB/INTERNSHIP OPPORTUNITIES Receptionist Immigration Law Firm in Midtown Manhattan is seeking an office receptionist. The main responsibilities include: Assisting clients that go to the office Organizing documents and files Mail management Assist attorneys and paralegals Handling the phones Maintain the office organized The candidate must be proficient in Spanish The position is on site in our office in Midtown Manhattan, full time, long term Salary is $20/$21 per hour and benefits: 401k, paid time off, medical, dental and vision Candidates must send resume to martha@grotaslaw.com SCHEDULER/RECEPTIONIST SCHEDULER/RECEPTIONIST OFFICE of CONGRESSWOMAN NYDIA VELAZQUEZ The Scheduler/Receptionist maintains the Congresswoman's official schedule, and related records. This position also acts as a liaison for the Congresswoman with the staff, public and other Members of Congress. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS: Prepares the daily schedule for the Congresswoman; Prepares detailed itineraries for the Congresswoman, including important numbers, locations and contact names; Prepares monthly projected schedules for the Congresswoman; Briefs the Congresswoman on all scheduling activities and requests of the Washington, D.C. and district offices; Schedules all staff meetings and briefings involving the Congresswoman; Reviews the Congresswoman's mail and invitations; Responds to all invitations, either by written correspondence or by personal telephone call; Maintains files of invitations that have been declined, accepted, or that are tentative/pending; Monitors the Congresswoman's incoming telephone calls, takes messages, and returns calls as requested; Places outgoing calls for the Congresswoman and maintains a record of calls; Maintains the Congresswoman's files, including notes, correspondence, and all information relating to travel; Acts as a liaison for constituents and other individuals when they visit the Congresswoman; Meets attendance requirements as established by the office; Works well under pressure and handles stress; Performs other duties as assigned. SKILLS AND KNOWLEDGE REQUIRED: Strong telephone skills; Strong oral and written communication skills in English and Spanish; Ability to exercise discretion and independent judgment with respect to prioritization of and recommendations on appointments; Proficiency in word processing; Strong organizational and filing skills; Thoroughness and careful attention to detail; Ability to perform essential job functions above; Ability to work cooperatively and courteously with others; Temperament to communicate with a variety of personalities in a tactful, pleasant, and professional manner; Knowledge of office administration, policies, practices, and procedures; Knowledge of office computer applications; Knowledge of office equipment &amp; machines; and WORKING CONDITIONS: Work is mainly performed in an office environment. Noise levels are usually moderate; and Ability to work in a small work station without an expectation of privacy. SALARY RANGE $50,000- $55,000 (depending on experience) Please send resume to evelyn.cruz@mail.house.gov FasTracKids Williamsburg FasTracKids Williamsburg - After School Instructor Seeking students in the education field who would like to teach in our enrichment/tutoring programs. Monday- Friday 2- 6pm Sunday 10-12pm What We Do Premiere Tutoring for Elementary and Middle School students Gifted and Talented Enrichment Programs Chess Lessons Host Holiday Camps What We Offer Competitive Salary Flexible Schedules Located in trendy Williamsburg, Brooklyn 20 minute walk from Boricua College Brooklyn Campus If you are interested in applying, please send your resume to Brittany@mastermindny.com SafeCamp SafeCamp is looking for 8-10 part time employees (with potential for full time hours) in the Bronx and around New York. SafeCamp is a Covid Testing + Health & Safety company that works directly with productions including TV shows, films, and events to ensure all who work there or in attendance are under covid compliance. We are currently looking to fill a variety of part time positions including testers and EMTs, both for daily productions and occasional events. There may be opportunities for additional hours for candidates whose work ethic and performance exceed expectations. The average work day starts early in the morning, includes setting up and swab testing a few hundred people, and the average shift is 4-5 hours. Qualifications : Candidates must demonstrate proven work ethic through resume and references, attention to detail, and ability to handle a flexible schedule including early hours and long days on your feet. The ideal candidate has hospitality experience and is flexible, personable, and enthusiastic. Must have reliable transportation to get to locations and be on time as locations can change day to day. Pay: $25/hour To apply, send your resume to hrsafecamp@gosafecamp.com BUSHWICK UNITED EARLY LEARNING CENTER Head Teacher position. Apply by emailing your cover letter and resume to MarilynA@bushwickunited.org Plan well-designed lessons that are aligned with the current units of study and culturally relevant pedagogy. Implement units of study and lesson plans in a thoughtful and intentional manner Identify goals for children Identify what staff and parents can do to help children achieve these goals Identify classroom materials needed to support the implementation of the curriculum towards achieving goals. Provide positive guidance for children Implement daily lesson plans. Lead various small group and center activities Delegate various academic and classroom-based responsibilities to assistant teacher and teacher aides. Complete and maintain observations and other running records Navigate Teaching Strategies GOLD online (assessment system). Provide consistent supervision that takes into account developmentally appropriate activities and health needs of the group and individual child. Understand individual student goals and connect those goals to academic activities. Work with small groups of children to reinforce lessons, providing one-on-one instruction to students and supervising students in the classroom. Create a warm and welcoming environment that includes a print-rich, and culturally responsive culture. Bushwick United provides: Health Benefits Union benefits 403B retirement saving plan Pensions Tuition reimbursement through NYS Quality Stars Handshake is the online job/internship posting board and on-campus recruiting platform. It offers jobs posted specifically for Boricua College students and alumni, as well as a broad job search function with thousands of job postings. You can even sign up to receive automatic notifications of new job postings that meet your preferences. In addition to being a job and internship search tool, Handshake is where students can sign up for events, workshops, read articles on career trends and access our on-campus recruitment program. LOG INTO HANDSHAKE No results found BROOKLYN CAMPUS 9 Graham Avenue Avenida de Puerto Rico Brooklyn, NY 11206 (718) 963-4112 BRONX CAMPUS 890 Washington Avenue Bronx, NY 10451 (347) 964-8600 Non-Discrimination Policy In compliance with Executive Order 11246, Boricua College is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Institution. Boricua College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, transgender orientation, genetic predisposition or carrier status, citizenship, disability, veteran or marital status in its student admissions, employment, access to programs and administration of educational and human resources policies. We are taking steps to make our website primarily compliant with Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) as published by the Web Accessibility Initiative (WAI) of the World Wide Web Consortium (W3C) If any information is not accessible to you, please contact one of the following: The Bronx: ‍         ‍ Mr. Teofilo Santiago (347) 964-8600 ‍    ‍ Brooklyn: ‍           ‍ Ms. Aurea Morales (718) 963-4112 ‍ CONTACT US VISIT US APPLY NOW Copyright © 2026 Boricua College"
